[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Counted by cause, its reports do not
share one issue, and the queued fix reaches only the largest group.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser does not close this ticket's reports. The booking-v3 form has a bug of its own.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The last column is the desk's own view: its ticket system still has one ticket. Each cause now
has a ticket of its own, linked below.

## `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first

Ticket: [parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/pdudzinsky/support-kb-4471/issues/1).

The shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants in day-first locales write the day first,
so the day and month come out swapped. This is the bug the queued fix is for.

The reports read as a one-day move stay here because the desk files by tenant. A swapped day and
month does not explain a one-day move. Read them again after the fix ships: if they keep coming,
they need a ticket of their own.

## `hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the month first

Ticket: [booking-v3 tells day-first tenants to type the month first](https://github.com/pdudzinsky/support-kb-4471/issues/2).

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it tells them,
month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not
change what this form prints, so these reports keep coming until the form changes. The fix is to
print the hint in the tenant's date order, as booking-v2 already does for its tenants.

Only reports through the form on a booking-v3 tenant belong here. The same tenants' app and email
reports are `parser`.

## Why one ticket hid this

- **Subjects do not tell the causes apart.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
  merges on subject alone, and both causes use the same subjects.
- **Intake tags are a guess.** Intake tags a report from the browser it came in on. The cause comes
  from the tenant and the channel. The `tagged as` column shows how often the two disagree, so do
  not count by tag.
- **The export repeats reports.** The ticket system exports pages that overlap. Count unique ids,
  not rows.

## What should change

- Keep the queued fix on the `parser` ticket, and schedule the `hint` fix on its own.
- Stop telling reporters that #4471 is one issue with one fix.
- Replace decision 0001 with a new record. It is accepted, so it stays as written until then.

